I don't have your current `PlantsList.jsx` file — it hasn't been shared in this conversation. Could you paste it so I can make the exact edit you're describing? I want to make sure I preserve your existing status-clear logic, `confirmingId` handling, focus behavior, and `aria-live` setup rather than guessing at the implementation.

That said, the technique itself is straightforward. When I see your file, the change will look something like this:

```jsx
// Add a counter ref
const announceCount = useRef(0);

// Wherever you set the status message:
announceCount.current += 1;
setStatusMessage(`${message} (${announceCount.current})`);
// The counter makes the string unique, so aria-live re-announces it.
```

A cleaner alternative that doesn't put a visible number in the text is to use the counter as a `key` on the status `<p>`, which forces React to unmount and remount it — triggering a fresh announcement:

```jsx
<p role="status" aria-live="polite" key={announceCount.current}>
  {statusMessage}
</p>
```

Both approaches work. The `key` version keeps the displayed text clean. Paste your file and I'll wire it in with everything else untouched.
